uenced by the Bolivarian Revolution initiated by Hugo Chávez."}, {"sourceSlug": "latin-american-socialism", "sourceName": "Latin American Socialism", "verb": "FRAMES", "targetSlug": "united-socialist-party-of-venezuela", "targetName": "United Socialist Party of Venezuela", "context": "The United Socialist Party of Venezuela has framed the discourse around socialism in Latin America, impacting regional politics."}], "places": [{"name": "Caracas, Venezuela", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Maracaibo, Venezuela", "role": "Major city"}, {"name": "Valencia, Venezuela", "role": "Political hub"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: United Socialist Party of Venezuela", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "united-socialist-party-of-venezuela"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q197864", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Socialist_Party_of_Venezuela"], "tags": ["Venezuela", "political party", "Americas", "Political Parties & Organizations", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "United Socialist Party of Venezuela contributed to the historical record of the Contemporary period. Key lasting impacts include: Shaped institutional landscape and community development. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "The PSUV has reshaped Venezuelan politics and inspired leftist movements throughout Latin America, while also facing significant backlash and criticism for its governance. Its influence has led to a polarized society and ongoing debates about socialism in the region.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-16T20:55:35Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#29533634781", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Socialist political party in venezuela. United Socialist Party of Venezuela is a political party in Caracas, established in 2007-03-24. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The United Socialist Party of Venezuela (PSUV), founded on March 24, 2007, in Caracas, epitomizes a significant shift in Venezuelan politics, particularly under the presidency of Hugo Chávez. This political party emerged as a cornerstone of the Bolivarian Revolution, a movement aimed at establishing socialism in Venezuela and promoting anti-imperialist sentiment within Latin America. The PSUV's ideology is rooted in a blend of Marxism and Bolivarianism, and it has played a crucial role in reshaping Venezuela's political landscape, making it a pivotal player in the region's contemporary history.

The PSUV was born from the consolidation of various leftist parties and movements, which were unified under Chávez's leadership. The party's formation was marked by its commitment to social justice, economic reform, and the redistribution of wealth. It gained substantial electoral victories, including a notable win in the 2006 presidential elections, where Chávez secured re-election with over 60% of the vote. The PSUV championed numerous social programs known as 'misiones,' aimed at alleviating poverty and expanding access to education and healthcare, significantly impacting millions of Venezuelans.

